	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Stranglethorn Vale is the great jungle of the south. It runs from the dark borders of {link:duskwood}Duskwood{/link} to a rocky cape where the land ends in the sea. Its trees are old and tall, its rivers are thick with crocolisks, and tigers, panthers, raptors and apes hunt beneath its green roof. Everywhere the vines have swallowed the stones of a fallen troll empire. No crown rules here. Goblins hold the port of {link:booty-bay}Booty Bay{/link}, the {link:horde}Horde{/link} keeps a camp on the western shore, hunters and deserters of the north pitch their tents in the hills, and the troll tribes wage their old wars in the ruins of their fathers.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[This was once the heart of the Gurubashi, the jungle trolls of the south. In ages before the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}, their empire stretched across these lands and far beyond. When the world broke, the empire lost much of its land to the sea, and its people turned in their need to dark worship. The priests of the Atal'ai called forth {link:hakkar}Hakkar{/link}, the blood god, in their capital of {link:zul-gurub}Zul'Gurub{/link}. The god fed on his worshippers, and at last the tribes rose against him and his priests. They cast Hakkar out and drove the Atal'ai into the swamps to the north. The Gurubashi Empire never recovered. Its tribes turned on one another, and the cities they had built were left to the jungle.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Stranglethorn has no master, and so it has many. The goblins of the {link:steamwheedle-cartel}Steamwheedle Cartel{/link} rule {link:booty-bay}Booty Bay{/link} at the southern tip, where every flag is welcome so long as it pays. Pirates of two rival fleets, the {red:blackwater-raiders}Blackwater Raiders{/red} and the {red:bloodsail-buccaneers}Bloodsail Buccaneers{/red}, fight for the waters of the cape. The {link:venture-company}Venture Company{/link} strips the northern hills for timber and crystal. In the north, a band of soldiers from {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} wages a desperate war against its own former colonel. On the western shore, the {link:horde}Horde{/link} has raised {link:grom-gol-base-camp}Grom'gol{/link}, and its {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link} envoys have come home to seek a lost son of their tribe. The famous hunter {link:hemet-nesingwary}Hemet Nesingwary{/link} has come to hunt the jungle's great beasts. And behind it all the trolls endure: the Bloodscalp, the Skullsplitter and the followers of the outcast {link:zanzil-the-outcast}Zanzil{/link}, each still at war with the others.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The goblins of {link:booty-bay}Booty Bay{/link}.{/b} Merchants, brokers and bruisers of the {link:steamwheedle-cartel}Steamwheedle Cartel{/link}, and the pirates of the Blackwater Raiders who drink in their taverns.
• {b}The Bloodsail Buccaneers.{/b} Rival pirates who have landed on the {link:wild-shore}Wild Shore{/link} and plot against the port.
• {b}The Gurubashi tribes.{/b} The Bloodscalp trolls in the north-west ruins, the Skullsplitter trolls in the central ruins, and the followers of {link:zanzil-the-outcast}Zanzil{/link} on the cape. Behind the walls of {link:zul-gurub}Zul'Gurub{/link}, older powers still stir.
• {b}The rebels and the deserters.{/b} {link:lieutenant-doren}Lieutenant Doren{/link}'s rebels in the north, and the men of {link:colonel-kurzen}Colonel Kurzen{/link} in the compound east of them.
• {b}The {link:horde}Horde{/link} at {link:grom-gol-base-camp}Grom'gol{/link}.{/b} {link:orcs}Orcs{/link} and {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link} trolls who guard the road of supply to {link:stonard}Stonard{/link} and the zeppelins to the north.
• {b}The hunters.{/b} {link:hemet-nesingwary}Hemet Nesingwary{/link} and his companions, camped by the northern river.
• {b}The ogres.{/b} The {link:mosh-ogg-ogre-mound}Mosh'Ogg{/link} clan holds a mound in the eastern mountains and the ruins of Mizjah.
• {b}The {link:naga}naga{/link}, the murlocs and the giants of the sea.{/b} They haunt the coasts, the sunken ruins and the reefs.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Empire.{/b} For long ages the Gurubashi ruled these jungles from {link:zul-gurub}Zul'Gurub{/link}. Their stone cities rose along the rivers and the coasts.
• {b}The Soulflayer.{/b} {link:hakkar}Hakkar{/link} was called into the world by the Atal'ai. His worship brought the empire to civil war, and his defeat left it shattered.
• {b}The Scattering.{/b} The tribes of the Gurubashi fought one another over what remained. The {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear tribe{/link} was driven from the jungle and went to the islands of the southern seas.
• {b}The Goblins.{/b} The goblins drove the trolls from a harbor at the southern tip of the jungle and built {link:booty-bay}Booty Bay{/link} upon it. No chronicle of the jungle records the year.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} Northerners have come in growing numbers: soldiers, hunters, miners and the {link:horde}Horde{/link}. None of them has tamed the Vale.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Jungle",
			text = [=[• Every people of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}, it is said, claims the waters of the holy spring on the western bluffs as a gift made sacred for its own kind alone.
• The soldiers of the rebel camp tell one another that the goblins of {link:booty-bay}Booty Bay{/link} drag drunken sailors aboard slave ships and carry them off to places no one names.
• A sickness called Stranglethorn Fever strikes down sailors on the cape. The only cure, the witch doctors say, is the heart of a white ape that no one can find.
• {link:hemet-nesingwary}Hemet Nesingwary{/link} has written a book of his hunts in the jungle. Its pages once blew away on the wind, and the jungle is still said to hide a few of them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Unrecorded",
			text = [=[No chronicle records the years in which the Gurubashi Empire rose, fell or scattered, or the year in which the goblins took {link:booty-bay}Booty Bay{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

