			key = "the-heads-that-spoke",
			title = "The Heads That Spoke",
			hint = [=[Bring the heads of the Bloodscalp chief and his witch doctor to Nimboya's cauldron.]=],
			unlock = {
				{ type = "quest", id = 588 },
			},
			text = [=[Nimboya feared the Bloodscalps had killed the boy, and he swore a curse of six hundred years on their chief if it were so. The heads of {link:gan-zulah}Gan'zulah{/link} and {link:nezzliok-the-dire}Nezzliok{/link} went into his cauldron, and the dead spoke. They bargained even then, and demanded trophies and blood before they would answer. At last Nezzliok told the truth. {link:yenniku}Yenniku{/link} lived, but he was no longer his own. The witch doctor {link:zanzil-the-outcast}Zanzil the Outcast{/link} held him, body and soul.]=],
		},
		{
			key = "saving-yenniku",
			title = "Saving Yenniku",
			hint = "Bring the lost son of the Darkspear home.",
			unlock = {
				{ type = "quest", id = 592 },
			},
			text = [=[Hope was faint after that, as small as the smallest insect, Nimboya said. But {link:kin-weelay}Kin'weelay{/link} learned from the spirits where the Mind's Eye lay. It was torn from the {link:ogres}ogre{/link} {link:mai-zoth}Mai'Zoth{/link}, and the witch doctor reshaped it into a gem that could hold a soul. With it {link:yenniku}Yenniku{/link} was stunned and his spirit taken from {link:zanzil-the-outcast}Zanzil{/link}'s grasp, and the gem was brought to {link:grom-gol-base-camp}Grom'gol{/link}. Nimboya had thought his mission hopeless. He promised that the tribe would sing of the deed and cut it in stone.]=],
